{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1531462-tc-scion","id":1531462,"title":"TC: Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-25T04:37:10-08:00","id":1531462,"title":"TC: Scion","content":"As was discussed in Discord a few days ago, I want to drop some ideas on how to Scion in TC.<br /> <br /> The character creation works as usual, and Scion is a template (so you have the usual attributes, askills, edges, skill tricks and specialties).<br /> <br /> My take on Legend would be similar to Inspiration, instead of a straight value trait, like Legend and Quantum.<br /> The Scion would have 3 Callings (1 to 5 dots), that define the Legend trait (the counting is a bit different but its ok).<br /> Callings Legend Tier<br /> 1 .............. 0 ............. Mundane<br /> 2 .............. 0 ............. Mundane<br /> 3 .............. 1 ............. Hero (must be 1 dot in each Calling)<br /> 4 .............. 2 ............. Hero<br /> 5 .............. 3 ............. Hero<br /> 6 .............. 4 ............. Hero<br /> 7 .............. 5 ............. Demigod<br /> 8 .............. 6 ............. Demigod<br /> 9 .............. 7 ............. Demigod<br /> 10 ............ 8 ............. Demigod<br /> 11 ............ 9 ............. God<br /> 12 ............ 10 ........... God<br /> 13 ............ 11 ........... God<br /> 14 ............ 12 ........... God<br /> 15 ............ 12 ........... God<br /> The characters raise their Legend by increasing their callings, and their Callings are increase by Deeds. Mundane people and Heroes can do many different heroic Deeds to increase their Callings, and the Deeds must be related somehow to the Calling being raised. Demigod must follow the apotheosis path to increase their Legend, and Gods need to increase their importance in the Pantheon to increase their Legend (so, basically as now in Scion).<br /> <br /> The Callings would work as the source of Scale to the Scion, by spending 1 Legend the Scion can increase her scale by half the calling dots (round up, so 1, 1, 2, 2, 3) when doing actions related to the Calling.<br /> <br /> Heroes have standard scale 1 and may increase by \u00bd calling by spending Legend.<br /> Demigods have standard scale 2 and may increase to full calling by imbuing Legend.<br /> Gods have scale 3 (4 for legend 12) and add to the calling when acting according to it (no imbueing)<br /> <br /> Scions have 1 Innate Purview and others granted by their Birthrights. Purviews are the way they can Dramatic Edit, basically they can use Legend to change the world around them within the limits of their Purviews. The grander the effect, the more Legend it requires, 1 point for a direct advantage (not scale) in a situation (grant enhancement, cause complication to the adversary, add tags to your attack, etc), 1 extra points to add scale to it (half the calling or 1 if not related to the callings), 1 extra point to make it last for the scene, 3 points to prevent certain death.<br /> <br /> Heroes spend Legend to create single action effects like booms<br /> Demigods imbue Legend to create effects (like booms) that last for the scene (like boons) or spend to gain the effect similar to Dominion<br /> Gods use freely effects like booms and imbue to gain effects like dominion and spend to gain the effects of Emminence of Purview.<br /> <br /> Instead of an Scale for each cathegory of effect, like Aberrant, there is an scale for each Calling. Some examples of when to use:<br /> Guardians can use scale to defend in any arena, but not to attack<br /> Warriors can only use scale on combat, both attacking and defending<br /> Sages can use when researching or using knowledge<br /> Tricksters can use to do tricks and being evasive<br /> and so on.<br /> <br /> Size and Speed scale are not changed, because they are about the physical aspect, so a warrior may be able to use their scale to lift objects, and a liminal or hunter to cross distances (escaping or hunting, respectively).<br /> <br /> Scions have 1 Innate Purview and others granted by their Birthrights. Purviews are the way they can Dramatic Edit, basically they can use Legend to change the world around them within the limits of their Purviews.<br /> <br /> Heroes spend Legend to create single action effects (like booms)<br /> Demigods imbue Legend to create effects that last for the scene (like boons) or spend to gain the effect similar to Dominion<br /> Gods use freely effects like booms and imbue to gain effects like dominion and spend to gain the effects of Emminence of Purview.<br /> \u200b<br /> Birthrights are special set of Edges that Scions only can have. They are the same ones as in Scion, but fashioned in 1-5 dot Edges. Creatures, Cult, Followers, Guides and Relics. Demigods gain access to Sanctum, and Gods to Creed.<br /> Birthrights can grant Scions access to Purviews and Callings, in addition to the many different effects they usually do, similar to edges.<br /> <br /> Booms and knacks are replaced by Gifts, you can have any number of Gifts, but they are not more powerful than the regular use of Legend, it just make it cheaper. There is no Dominion Boom or Emminence Boom, only effects that can be done more efficiently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-26-2024, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T15:59:34-08:00","id":1531484,"title":"","content":"With the difference in Scale between Scion and Trinity Continuum, I think you can tackle gaining Scale in a slightly different way. Otherwise, Demigods would hardly compare to many Novas.<br /> <br /> Heroes: Tier 2. Start at Base Scale 1, Can increase Scale by an amount equal to (Calling/2, rounded up) by Spending 1 Legend so long as it's aligned with the Calling. Alternatively, can Imbue Legend instead when performing an action associated with one of their Legendary Titles.<br /> <br /> Demigods: Tier 3. Start at Base Scale 2 in all realms, can choose between Size Scale 1 and 2 reflexively because I think its funny :V. Can Spend 1 Legend to add their (Lowest Calling/2) Scale to ANY action. Can imbue 1 Legend to add (Calling/2) Scale to an action related to that Calling, or gain that Scale for free with an action that aligns with a Legendary Title.<br /> <br /> Gods: Tier 3 (4?). Start at Base Scale 3 in all realms, or 4 at Legend 12. Can spend 1 Legend to add Scale to any action like Demigods can, and can Imbue 1 Legend with a feat tied to a Calling, Legendary Title or Purview to add (Relevant Calling) Scale to the action. This means that the highest typical Scale a God could achieve is 9, which works within the extended Scale ranks seen in Aberrant. They're not altering the Solar System on a whim, but they are definitely capable of some pretty insane feats at a base level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-25T17:13:52-08:00","id":1531485,"title":"","content":"That is an interesting approach.<br /> i personally would stay away from virtues and legendary titles because they are too descriptive and at same time to generic.<br /> <br /> Heroes have standard scale 1 and may increase by \u00bd calling by spending Legend.<br /> Demigods have standard scale 2 and may increase to full calling by imbuing Legend.<br /> Gods have scale 3 (4 for legend 12) and add to the calling when acting according to it (no imbueing)<br /> <br /> When using Purviews<br /> Heroes spend Legend to create single action effects (like booms)<br /> Demigods imbue Legend to create effects that last for the scene (like boons) or spend to gain the effect similar to Dominion<br /> Gods use freely effects like booms and imbue to gain effects like dominion and spend to gain the effects of Emminence of Purview.<br /> <br /> Instead of an Scale for each aspect, like Aberrant, there is an scale for each Calling. Some examples of when to use:<br /> Guardians can use scale to defend in any arena, but not to attack<br /> Warriors can only use scale on combat, both attacking and defending<br /> Sages can use when researching or using knowledge<br /> Tricksters can use to do tricks and being evasive<br /> and so on.<br /> <br /> Size and Speed scale are not changed, because they are about the physical aspect, so a warrior may be able to use their scale to lift objects, and a liminal or hunter to cross distances (escaping or hunting, respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-26-2024, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-27T21:05:07-08:00","id":1531665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1531462-tc-scion?p=1531485#post1531485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an interesting approach.<br /> i personally would stay away from virtues and legendary titles because they are too descriptive and at same time to generic.<br /> <br /> Heroes have standard scale 1 and may increase by \u00bd calling by spending Legend.<br /> Demigods have standard scale 2 and may increase to full calling by imbuing Legend.<br /> Gods have scale 3 (4 for legend 12) and add to the calling when acting according to it (no imbueing)<br /> <br /> When using Purviews<br /> Heroes spend Legend to create single action effects (like booms)<br /> Demigods imbue Legend to create effects that last for the scene (like boons) or spend to gain the effect similar to Dominion<br /> Gods use freely effects like booms and imbue to gain effects like dominion and spend to gain the effects of Emminence of Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Legendary Titles are pretty cool, and fit well with Scion's world of feats defining your growth on the path to apotheosis, but fair enough.<br /> <br /> Regarding Purviews, what are your thoughts regarding Gods transforming their Purviews into Innate ones? Would there be a bonus for any internalized Purviews like in 2e, or is the sole benefit of internalizing not needing a Birthright to use that Purview like in 1e? Actually, would you keep the Enhancement bonus for combining an innate Purview with a Birthright that grants the same Purview? It makes sense to me since by &quot;doubling up&quot; to give a bonus like that since you are giving up diversity in abilities for a greater emphasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T00:39:19-08:00","id":1531669,"title":"","content":"Legendary Titles are not bad, but they are based in the callings, so you could keep only the callings to work. It\u2019s not that simple, but It think it\u2019s a bit overdoing. Same for Virtues, they end up as additional things you must think when you are imagining what would the character do, they are interesting, but they are one more thing in the way, you already have Fatebonds and Callings defining how you better behave. I got a bit overdone by Scion rules on how to play MY OWN character, Callings being an benefit of playing your role in legends and Fatebonding pushing you to the legend even against your will are enough.<br /> <br /> Now, the innate purviews I like the idea of doubling up. After all, instead of more versatile you are choosing to be more focused. It\u2019s not that you gain free scale, but an enhancement when using your doubled up purview is great.<br /> <br /> Gods turning everything into innate (it\u2019s not everything, only what you have booms related) is a bit odd, as it makes you get rid of your birthrights, something I would not do. I understand the reason, but would not do it that way. I like the idea of 4 innate purviews for gods, I could even see demigods having 3 innate purviews, but understand why not (and agree on that).<br /> <br /> In 1e there was a rule on using physical traits as sources of purviews, like the missing eye of Odin giving him access to magic, and the missing hand of Tyr giving justice, I would bring it to the game. It\u2019s a mark of the character you could erase to be easier to hide, but instead you keep it to retain a purview when creating avatars and incarnations. It must be related to your legend, being caused in the legend or used somehow in the legend, so not something you start with, but at demigod tier it become available. Also it doesn\u2019t need to be missing body parts, you may have a fiery hair that gives you access to Fire purview or the green eyes of a lier that gives access to Deception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-04T23:38:19-07:00","id":1535162,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> Plot question - How would you reconcile <b>TC Scion</b> with <b>TC Aegis</b>? All the Heroes in Aegis - <i>Olympians, Champions and Oracles</i> - are really Scions of the Gods 'in heavens'? Ambrosia is 'essence' of Godhood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-05T06:39:45-07:00","id":1535170,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my idea here is more about making Scion closer to what I think is a better system\u2026 Scion is all about reaching godhood, the characters want to become gods, they want to build their mantles and want to leave humanity behind. I think it\u2019s ok, but I dot like it, I prefere the balance of Divine and Mundane (closer to Part Time Gods setting), and as Scion is, it\u2019s really hard to have any kind of counterpoint.<br /> <br /> But I would make Legend as an independent Source, and so Olympians as Quantum users would not be true Legendary beings. Gods, demigods and heroes would be another set of characters. If Legend is one of the 3 sources, it would be closer to Flux, with all the narrative aspect, so if you want to force, Champions would be the closest to true gods, with Olympians (and their elemental powers closer to Titans and Primordials) and Oracles related to magic (not divine magic, arcane magic by DnD standards).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name